I'll build this session chair's run-of-show as a Rhylthyme program, following the source text carefully.

**Analysis of the workflow:**

- **Setup phase** (before the room opens): AV desk line check (30 min) → projector test (15 min, after desk) → lapel pack check (10 min, after projector) → load first deck (10 min, after lapel check).
- **Session phase** (chair opens → three speakers with transitions):
  - Chair opens (5 min, after first deck load).
  - Speaker 1 (30 min) → questions 1 (7 min plan, 5–10 variable).
  - Load deck 2 (5 min, after questions 1).
  - Changeover 2 (5 min, unclip/clip lapel pack).
  - Speaker 2 (30 min) → questions 2 (7 min plan, 5–10 variable).
  - Load deck 3 (5 min, after questions 2) — *concurrent* with coffee going out.
  - Changeover 3 (5 min, after foyer is clear).
  - Speaker 3 (30 min) → questions 3 (10 min plan, 5–15 variable).
  - Chair closes (5 min).
- **Catering**: Set coffee station at t=−90 min (30 min duration) → coffee out when questions 2 end (20 min) → clear foyer (10 min).
- **Strike**: Strike AV desk when chair closes (20 min).

**Resource constraints:** projector, lapel pack, AV desk, lectern, foyer.

**Key dependencies:**
- Deck loads can only happen when the projector is not in use (not during talks).
- Lapel pack transitions must happen between talks.
- Coffee service competes with speaker 3 setup.
- Everything done by 10:30 (630 minutes from start).

